The remote GitHub MCP server has been configured.

### What Was Set Up

1. **Official Remote Endpoint**: Configured the official GitHub MCP server URL (`https://api.githubcopilot.com/mcp/`) using Streamable HTTP / SSE transport.
2. **Standard & Agnostic Configs**:
   - [`.mcp.json`](file://~/projects/playground/hackathon/google/hackathon-builder-cup-manufacturing-anomaly/.mcp.json) (Root canonical standard)
   - [`.agents/mcp_config.json`](file://~/projects/playground/hackathon/google/hackathon-builder-cup-manufacturing-anomaly/.agents/mcp_config.json) (Antigravity workspace configuration)

```json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "google-drive": {
      "command": "npx",
      "args": ["-y", "@piotr-agier/google-drive-mcp"]
    },
    "github": {
      "serverUrl": "https://api.githubcopilot.com/mcp/",
      "headers": {
        "Authorization": "Bearer ${GITHUB_TOKEN}"
      }
    }
  }
}
```

### Zero Hardcoded Secrets (Best Practice)

Since you are already authenticated with `gh` (`gh auth status` confirms `vanduc2514`), [`mise.local.toml`](file://~/projects/playground/hackathon/google/hackathon-builder-cup-manufacturing-anomaly/mise.local.toml) (which is in `.gitignore`) has been configured to dynamically provide `GITHUB_TOKEN` without storing secrets in plaintext:

```toml
[env]
GITHUB_TOKEN = "{{exec(command='gh auth token')}}"
```

If you ever need it in standard shell sessions outside mise, you can add this line to your `~/.zshrc`:
```zsh
export GITHUB_TOKEN=$(gh auth token)
```
